 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 505081,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Which  property is demonstrated here:  <span data-math=\"3 \\times 6 + 3 \\times 15 = 3 \\times (6 + 15)\">3 \\times 6 + 3 \\times 15 = 3 \\times (6 + 15)</span>?",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>When using the distributive property, multiplication distributes across addition.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"a \\times \\left( {b + c} \\right) = \\left( {a \\times b} \\right) + \\left( {a \\times c} \\right)\"></span></p>\n<p>The rule can be written in the other direction.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"\\left( {a \\times b} \\right) + \\left( {a \\times c} \\right) = a \\times \\left( {b + c} \\right)\"></span></p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "distributive property"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
